---
/**
 * The campaign hero band (04 §3), rendered by audience rather than by
 * referrer.
 *
 * THE SAME BAND `withCampaignHero` BUILDS, AND THAT IS THE POINT rather than
 * a coincidence. src/lib/tier/hero-band.ts renders this band on the home
 * page as an HTML string spliced in by HTMLRewriter -- a string because
 * HTMLRewriter's `element.after()` takes one, not an Astro component, so a
 * prerendered static page can carry a referrer-matched line without an
 * on-demand route. `/fit` already reads its grant on every request, so there
 * is no equivalent constraint here and this component can be the real thing.
 * The two are kept in step BY HAND, not by one calling the other: a change
 * to the class list, the element, or the padding belongs in both files, or
 * the band the home page shows and the band `/fit` shows drift apart
 * visually with nothing to catch it.
 *
 * NO `escapeHtml` HERE, AND THAT IS NOT AN OMISSION. `hero-band.ts` inserts
 * its band with `{ html: true }`, so it has to escape `heroLine` itself
 * before it is anything but markup -- see `escapeHtml`'s own docblock there.
 * Astro escapes every `{expression}` in its template by default, which is
 * what `{line}` below is, so an equivalent call here would double-escape the
 * line rather than protect it. One line is operator-typed into KV either
 * way; the two renderers just protect it through different mechanisms.
 *
 * NO `Vary` AND NO `no-store` ON EITHER FIT SURFACE, and the reason is not
 * that these responses happen to go uncached. The band here is a
 * deterministic function of the URL: `/fit` carries the token in its query
 * string and the permalink carries the report id in its path, so a cache
 * keyed on the URL cannot serve one audience's band to another. That is
 * exactly what `withCampaignHero`'s own `no-store` paragraph is about on the
 * home page, where the band varies on `Referer` -- a request header that is
 * not in the cache key, which is what makes an intermediary able to hand one
 * visitor's band to the next. A reader arriving here from that paragraph
 * asks this question immediately, so it is answered here rather than left to
 * the inference that the surfaces are merely uncached today.
 */
interface Props {
  line: string;
}
const { line } = Astro.props;
---

{line !== '' && (
  <section data-campaign-hero class="border-b border-rule bg-accent-ground/10">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1440px] px-5 py-4 lg:px-10">
      <p class="text-small text-ink">{line}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
)}
